+
+Concretely:
+
+1. **Linking happens on the way in, in `Log.js`.** Every `{"file": "..."}` line calls `file(name)`. `file()` tests the name against `CHILD = /^([^/]+)\/page\.(jsonl|js)$/`. A match (e.g. `"kid/page.jsonl"` or `"kid/page.js"`) calls `link_child(name)`, which calls `child_file(name)` to split it into `dir` ("kid") and `kind` ("jsonl" or "js"), records `this.child_kinds.set(dir, kind)`, and — if not already there — sets `this.children.set(dir, null)` (`Log.js`, `file()`/`child_file()`/`link_child()`). So by the time anyone routes, the page's `children` Map already has an entry for `kid`, and `child_kinds` remembers whether it's a `.jsonl` or `.js` child.
