+- At line 312, `swap_link` calls `history.pushState({}, "", url + link.hash)` — so the browser address bar and history actually change to that URL when it differs from the current one.
+- It wires `popstate` (line 291, 313: `on_pop`) so that hitting Back fires `close()`, which removes the swapped-in shell and restores the hidden siblings (line 293-298).
+- The in-page "Back" button (line 303) calls `back()` (line 290), which checks `location.pathname === url`: if the address is still showing the swap, it calls `history.back()` (letting popstate do the closing); otherwise it calls `close()` directly — this covers the case where the swap happened without a URL change (e.g., same path already).
+
+So "keeps a doc routed" means: the swap is never just a visual overlay — it's registered as a real history entry at `<page>/md/<doc>/`, so reload lands back on the same doc (doc/open.md's file-loading path re-renders it) and Back/forward navigation correctly opens and closes it via the `popstate` listener, per the comment at lines 278-280.
+
